@.str.112 = private unnamed_addr constant [14 x i8] c"compare_total\00", align 1
@doc_compare_total = internal constant [1023 x i8] c"compare_total($self, /, other, context=None)\0A--\0A\0ACompare two operands using their abstract representation rather than\0Atheir numerical value.  Similar to the compare() method, but the result\0Agives a total ordering on Decimal instances.  Two Decimal instances with\0Athe same numeric value but different representations compare unequal\0Ain this ordering:\0A\0A    >>> Decimal('12.0').compare_total(Decimal('12'))\0A    Decimal('-1')\0A\0AQuiet and signaling NaNs are also included in the total ordering. The result\0Aof this function is Decimal('0') if both operands have the same representation,\0ADecimal('-1') if the first operand is lower in the total order than the second,\0Aand Decimal('1') if the first operand is higher in the total order than the\0Asecond operand. See the specification for details of the total order.\0A\0AThis operation is unaffected by context and is quiet: no flags are changed\0Aand no rounding is performed. As an exception, the C version may raise\0AInvalidOperation if the second operand cannot be converted exactly.\0A\0A\00", align 16
